      "statusChangeID": "5d3fe0b3096d9d44b1446224",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "complete",
      "value": "See additional note below. Fixed in an upcoming build.\n\nGoing forward, if you set Far Limit to 0 (or less) you will mute all avatar sources within that VRC_PlayerAudioOverride.\n\nA Far Limit with really small values will probably sound different with and without ONSP applied, this is normal and expected.\n\nSetting the Gain to negative, as before, mutes avatar audio. This is true whether or not ONSP is applied, and this is probably what most users would use.\n\nRegardless, we strongly recommend using a VRC_SpatialAudioSource with all audio sources on avatars.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
